course: dictionary
lesson: 2964
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Dropping can mean letting something fall, becoming lower, or the poo of an animal. The words around it, the context, show you which meaning to use.
explain: «Temperatures are dropping every night.» Temperatures cannot fall off anything, so dropping here means getting lower. «Mum is dropping me off at school.» Dropping off means taking someone somewhere in a car and leaving them there.
explain: «Rangers study droppings to learn which animals live in a place.» Droppings here means animal poo. Scientists use it as a clue, but animal droppings can carry germs, so never touch them, and always wash your hands afterwards.
fact: Dropping is a verb: drop, drops, dropped, dropping.
fact: Dropping can mean letting something fall, or falling.
fact: Dropping can also mean becoming lower or less, like dropping temperatures.
fact: Droppings are the poo of animals and birds, and the word is usually used in the plural.
fact: «Wombats» are the only animals known to make cube-shaped droppings, which do not roll away.
exercise: «Rangers study droppings to learn what animals eat.» What are droppings in this sentence? | Bits of wood for a fire | Leaves blown off a tree | *Animal poo | Pebbles from a stream
exercise: Mum says, «I'm dropping you off at school.» What does dropping off mean? | Getting lower in price | *Taking you somewhere in a car and leaving you there | Falling over | Letting go of a ball
exercise: «Temperatures are dropping every night.» What does dropping mean here? | Lifting up | *Getting lower | Growing taller | Shouting louder
test: «A house mouse leaves droppings like grains of rice.» What are droppings? | Small seeds for birds | Crumbs of cheese | Grains of sand | *Animal poo
test: «Prices are dropping in the shop this week.» What does dropping mean? | Becoming higher | Staying exactly the same | Being thrown away | *Becoming lower
exam: Rangers study droppings to find out which animals live in a place. What is the main reason they do this? | To win a prize for the best photo | To make paper from the droppings | To feed the chicks in a nest | *To find out which animals live there and what they eat
